From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jahred Love <jahred.love@aircall.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:55:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep libpeer's output off standard output

What: sctp.c printed a line to standard output whenever a data channel
opened, mdns.c printed when its buffer was too small, and libpeer's own
log lines went to standard output too.

Now those two go through libpeer's logging, at debug and warning level,
and its logging writes to standard error, so LOG_LEVEL governs all of it
and standard output is left to the program. (The printf calls in
dtls_srtp.c are inside #if 0.)

Why: a Jello program's standard output is its own; wobblertc builds
libpeer with logging off, and nothing should reach standard output.

This patch applies after 0004.

Like libpeer, this patch is under the MIT licence.
---
 src/mdns.c  | 2 +-
 src/sctp.c  | 2 +-
 src/utils.h | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mdns.c b/src/mdns.c
index 6d7881c..d2c0e59 100644
--- a/src/mdns.c
+++ b/src/mdns.c
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ static int mdns_build_query(const char* hostname, uint8_t* buf, int size) {
 
   total_size = sizeof(DnsHeader) + strlen(hostname) + sizeof(DnsQuery) + 2;
   if (size < total_size) {
-    printf("buf size is not enough");
+    LOGW("buf size is not enough");
     return -1;
   }
 
diff --git a/src/sctp.c b/src/sctp.c
index 644f8d8..3b57199 100644
--- a/src/sctp.c
+++ b/src/sctp.c
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ void sctp_parse_data_channel_open(Sctp* sctp, uint16_t sid, char* data, size_t l
     label_str[label_length] = '\0';
 
     // Log or process the DATA_CHANNEL_OPEN message
-    printf("DATA_CHANNEL_OPEN: Label=%s, sid=%d\n", label_str, sid);
+    LOGD("DATA_CHANNEL_OPEN: Label=%s, sid=%d", label_str, sid);
 
     // Add stream mapping
     sctp_add_stream_mapping(sctp, label_str, sid);
diff --git a/src/utils.h b/src/utils.h
index 72040ae..4519af5 100644
--- a/src/utils.h
+++ b/src/utils.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ void peer_log(char* level_tag, const char* file_name, int line_number, const cha
   peer_log(level_tag, __FILE__, __LINE__, fmt, ##__VA_ARGS__)
 #else
 #define LOG_PRINT(level_tag, fmt, ...) \
-  fprintf(stdout, "%s\t%s\t%d\t" fmt "\n", level_tag, __FILE__, __LINE__, ##__VA_ARGS__)
+  fprintf(stderr, "%s\t%s\t%d\t" fmt "\n", level_tag, __FILE__, __LINE__, ##__VA_ARGS__)
 #endif
 
 #if LOG_LEVEL >= LEVEL_DEBUG
